## Language format v1.2.0
## Super Duper Vanilla Shaderpack Language File
## Optimized with Sodium-style didactic tooltips & visual/performance indicators

## Profiles
profile.comment = Selects a performance profile balancing visual fidelity and framerate.\n\n§e[Visual] §fToggles and tunes effects across all rendering passes.\n§a[Performance] §fPotato (fastest) to Ultra (highest quality).\n§b[Tip] §7Medium is the recommended baseline for most players.

profile.POTATO = Potato
profile.POTATO.comment = Maximum performance mode for low-end hardware and integrated graphics.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDisables dynamic shadows, volumetric lighting, godrays, SSAO, reflections, and bloom.\n§a[Performance: Very Low Load] §fMaximum FPS on laptops and budget PCs.\n§b[Tip] §7Ideal for handhelds or high refresh-rate competitive play.

profile.LOW = Low
profile.LOW.comment = Lightweight visual enhancements with minimal framerate overhead.\n\n§e[Visual] §fEnables fast godrays, basic sunlight shadows, subtle bloom, and simple caustics.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fRuns smoothly on entry-level dedicated GPUs.\n§b[Tip] §7Great balance if you want shadows without sacrificing speed.

profile.MEDIUM = Medium (Recommended)
profile.MEDIUM.comment = The standard Super Duper Vanilla experience with rich atmospheric lighting.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFull volumetric lighting, soft shadows, SSAO, volumetric clouds, and TAA.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fOptimized for modern mainstream gaming PCs.\n§b[Tip] §7Provides the best aesthetic balance as intended by the developers.

profile.HIGH = High
profile.HIGH.comment = Enhanced fidelity with deeper surface detail and refined reflections.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher shadow resolution, rough reflections, crisp sharpening, and high godray steps.\n§c[Performance: Heavy Impact] §fRecommended for mid-to-high-end dedicated graphics cards.\n§b[Tip] §7Pairs well with 1080p and 1440p displays.

profile.ULTRA = Ultra
profile.ULTRA.comment = Maximum graphical preset with uncompromising visual excellence.\n\n§e[Visual] §f4096p ultra-crisp shadows, maximum godray raymarching steps, and deep water caustics.\n§4[Performance: Very Heavy Impact] §fDesigned for high-end GPUs.\n§b[Tip] §7Best for cinematic recording and screenshot photography.

## Debug Screen
screen.DEBUG = HyperDuper Vanilla v1.4.0
screen.DEBUG.comment = §dHyperDuper Vanilla §7(Fork of §bSuper Duper Vanilla§7 by §2Eldeston§7 & §9FlameRender Studios§7).\n\n§e[About] §fCrafted with AI vibecoding for high-velocity shader experimentation.\n§e[Status] §fProvided AS IS without warranty; maintenance may be inactive.\n§a[Performance: None] §fClick to open debug options.
    option.COLOR_MODE = Color Mode
    option.COLOR_MODE.comment = Overrides block albedo colors to inspect lighting, materials, and foliage isolation.\n\n§e[Visual] §fWhite/Black mode neutralizes textures; Foliage mode highlights plant life.\n§a[Performance: None] §fDebug visualization only.\n§b[Tip] §7Keep OFF for normal gameplay.
        value.COLOR_MODE.0 = OFF
        value.COLOR_MODE.1 = White Mode
        value.COLOR_MODE.2 = Black Mode
        value.COLOR_MODE.3 = Foliage Mode

    option.NOISE_SPEED = Noise Speed
    option.NOISE_SPEED.comment = Controls how rapidly the temporal blue noise pattern shifts each frame.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAffects how noise grain dissolves when using Temporal Anti-Aliasing (TAA).\n§a[Performance: None] §fTemporal noise calculation tweak.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 8 provides smooth noise convergence.

    option.VOXY_DEBUG = Voxy LOD Debug
    option.VOXY_DEBUG.comment = Diagnostic overlay for inspecting Voxy Level-Of-Detail (LOD) distant terrain integration.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHighlights LOD chunk borders, lightmap coordinates, or surface normal vectors.\n§a[Performance: None] §fShader debug pass.\n§b[Tip] §7Useful for mod developers and pack debugging.
        value.VOXY_DEBUG.0 = OFF
        value.VOXY_DEBUG.1 = Boundary
        value.VOXY_DEBUG.2 = Lightmap UV
        value.VOXY_DEBUG.3 = Normals

## Post-Processing Screen
screen.POST = Post-Processing
screen.POST.comment = Lens, camera, anti-aliasing, sharpening, and stylized outline effects.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAccess camera bloom, depth of field, tonemapping, and outlines.\n§a[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fVaries by enabled sub-effects.
    option.OUTLINES = Block Outlines
    option.OUTLINES.comment = Draws stylized borders around block edges and silhouette boundaries.\n\n§e[Visual] §fStandard gives classic ink lines; Dungeons gives Minecraft Dungeons cel-shaded style.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fSingle-pass normal and depth edge detector.\n§b[Tip] §7Looks fantastic for an illustrated or retro adventure aesthetic!
        value.OUTLINES.0 = OFF
        value.OUTLINES.1 = Standard
        value.OUTLINES.2 = Dungeons

    option.OUTLINE_BRIGHTNESS = Outline Brightness
    option.OUTLINE_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Controls the brightness and luminance tone of block outlines.\n\n§e[Visual] §fNegative values produce dark ink outlines; positive values produce luminous highlights.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor scalar adjustment.\n§b[Tip] §7Set to -1.00 for bold dark comic outlines, or +1.00 for glowing edges.

    option.OUTLINE_PIXEL_SIZE = Outline Thickness
    option.OUTLINE_PIXEL_SIZE.comment = Adjusts outline width in screen pixels.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce thicker, bolder contours around blocks.\n§a[Performance: None] §fKernel radius scalar.\n§b[Tip] §71 to 2 pixels is recommended for clean, modern readability.

    option.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE = Targeted Block Outline
    option.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE.comment = Style and rendering mode of the selection outline around targeted blocks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fInverted inverts the scene value beneath the line (like Vanilla crosshairs/indicators), guaranteeing high visibility against any background. Black and White offer classic solid colors.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLine rasterization mode.\n§b[Tip] §7Inverted is recommended for optimal visibility in dark caves and bright biomes alike.
        value.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE.0 = OFF
        value.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE.1 = Inverted (Vanilla)
        value.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE.2 = Solid Black
        value.TARGET_OUTLINE_MODE.3 = Solid White

    option.TARGET_OUTLINE_THICKNESS = Targeted Outline Width
    option.TARGET_OUTLINE_THICKNESS.comment = Adjusts the thickness of the targeted block selection outline in screen pixels.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values expand the wireframe border width for improved readability.\n§a[Performance: None] §fScreen-space vertex extrusion.\n§b[Tip] §72.0 or 2.5 pixels provides crisp, bold visibility without obscuring the block.

    option.RETRO_FILTER = Retro Pixel Filter
    option.RETRO_FILTER.comment = Snaps screen pixel coordinates to simulate vintage 90s console gaming.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates an authentic low-resolution pixelated look.\n§a[Performance: None] §fUV coordinate quantization.\n§b[Tip] §7Works best when lowering your render resolution for true nostalgia.

    option.ANTI_ALIASING = Anti-Aliasing (AA)
    option.ANTI_ALIASING.comment = Smooths jagged block edges and eliminates crawling shimmer during camera motion.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFXAA provides fast edge blur; TAA removes temporal shimmering and denoises lighting.\n§a[Performance: Low] §fFXAA has negligible cost; TAA has low-to-moderate cost.\n§b[Tip] §7Recommended: TAA or Lite TAA+FXAA for stable, noise-free raytracing.
        value.ANTI_ALIASING.0 = OFF
        value.ANTI_ALIASING.1 = FXAA
        value.ANTI_ALIASING.2 = TAA
        value.ANTI_ALIASING.3 = Lite TAA + FXAA

    option.SHARPEN_FILTER = Image Sharpening
    option.SHARPEN_FILTER.comment = Applies an intelligent contrast-adaptive sharpening filter to the final frame.\n\n§e[Visual] §fEnhances texture clarity, block edges, and counteracts any TAA softness.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fFast 3x3 sharpening kernel.\n§b[Tip] §7Recommended whenever TAA is active for crisp, punchy visuals.

    ## Camera Screen
    screen.CAMERA = Camera & Lens
    screen.CAMERA.comment = Cinematic optical effects including depth of field, bloom, motion blur, and lens flare.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSimulates physical camera optics and lens properties.\n§a[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fModerate when Depth of Field is enabled.
        option.DOF = Depth of Field (DoF)
        option.DOF.comment = Blurs background or foreground objects outside the player's focal distance.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates beautiful cinematic bokeh blur focusing on the crosshair target.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fCircle-of-confusion bokeh blur pass.\n§b[Tip] §7Amazing for close-up inspection, screenshot photography, and immersion!

        option.DOF_STRENGTH = DoF Blur Strength
        option.DOF_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the maximum radius and intensity of the depth of field blur.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher settings produce stronger, dreamier background blur.\n§a[Performance: None] §fBlur kernel radius multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §7Level 1 or 2 provides a natural, subtle photographic focus.

        option.BLOOM = Bloom Glow
        option.BLOOM.comment = Causes bright light sources and glowing surfaces to emit a soft, radiant aura.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSun, torches, lanterns, lava, and glowing blocks bleed light into the air.\n§a[Performance: Low] §fDownscaled Gaussian blur pyramid.\n§b[Tip] §7Adds atmospheric warmth and brilliance to caves and nighttime scenery.

        option.BLOOM_STRENGTH = Bloom Intensity
        option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment = Controls how brightly and far glowing light bleeds across the screen.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create a more luminous, heavenly glow.\n§a[Performance: None] §fBloom composite brightness multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 0.75 gives vibrant radiance without washing out the screen.

        option.MOTION_BLUR = Motion Blur
        option.MOTION_BLUR.comment = Blurs the screen along camera rotation velocity vectors during fast turns.\n\n§e[Visual] §fProduces smooth, fluid cinematic movement when looking around.\n§a[Performance: Low] §fVelocity vector directional blur pass.\n§b[Tip] §7Makes 60 FPS gameplay feel significantly smoother.

        option.MOTION_BLUR_STRENGTH = Motion Blur Strength
        option.MOTION_BLUR_STRENGTH.comment = Adjusts the intensity of the camera motion blur effect.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce longer streaks during rapid head turns.\n§a[Performance: None] §fVelocity scaling factor.\n§b[Tip] §7Keep between 0.50 and 1.00 for comfortable, non-disorienting motion.

        option.LENS_FLARE = Lens Flare
        option.LENS_FLARE.comment = Produces anamorphic optical flare streaks when looking towards the sun or moon.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCinematic horizontal light flares radiating from bright celestial bodies.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fLightweight screen-space lens flare pass.\n§b[Tip] §7Gives outdoor vistas a grand cinematic movie aesthetic.

        option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH = Lens Flare Intensity
        option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH.comment = Adjusts the brightness and visibility of celestial lens flare streaks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make the optical lens glare more vivid.\n§a[Performance: None] §fIntensity scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Set to 1.00 for balanced, elegant solar flares.

        option.VIGNETTE = Vignette
        option.VIGNETTE.comment = Subtly darkens the outer corners and borders of the screen.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDraws visual focus toward the center of your view like a real camera lens.\n§a[Performance: None] §fFast radial distance shading.\n§b[Tip] §7Enhances immersion and depth perception during gameplay.

        option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH = Vignette Intensity
        option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH.comment = Adjusts the darkness and reach of the corner vignette shading.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values increase edge darkening.\n§a[Performance: None] §fRadial falloff scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7A subtle value of 0.50 to 1.00 is pleasant for long play sessions.

        option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION = Chromatic Aberration
        option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.comment = Simulates optical color fringing caused by real camera lens refraction.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSplits red, green, and blue color channels slightly toward the screen edges.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fSub-pixel color offset sampling.\n§b[Tip] §7Adds subtle analog camera charm to the periphery of your view.

        option.ABERRATION_PIXEL_SIZE = Aberration Offset Size
        option.ABERRATION_PIXEL_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the pixel separation distance between color channels.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create more pronounced color separation.\n§a[Performance: None] §fOffset distance scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Values of 2 to 4 pixels give a tasteful, realistic lens fringe.

    ## Tonemap Screen
    screen.TONEMAP = Tonemapping & Color
    screen.TONEMAP.comment = Color grading controls including contrast, saturation, exposure, and color tinting.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSculpt the color mood, brightness, and warmth of the world.\n§a[Performance: None] §fArithmetic color grading with zero FPS impact.
        option.CONTRAST = Contrast
        option.CONTRAST.comment = Adjusts the separation between dark shadows and bright highlights.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make shadows deeper and highlights punchier.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor curve exponent.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 1.00 gives balanced, natural dynamic range.

        option.SATURATION = Saturation
        option.SATURATION.comment = Controls the richness and intensity of colors throughout the world.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make foliage, skies, and blocks deeply colorful and vibrant.\n§a[Performance: None] §fChroma vector scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Raise to 1.15 if you prefer extra colorful, lush scenery!

        option.WHITE_POINT = White Point
        option.WHITE_POINT.comment = Controls the maximum scene luminance mapped to pure display white.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values preserve more detail in intense sunlit highlights.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTonemap curve ceiling.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 2.0 provides smooth highlight rolloff.

        option.SHOULDER_STRENGTH = Highlight Shoulder
        option.SHOULDER_STRENGTH.comment = Controls how aggressively ultra-bright highlights roll off and compress.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPrevents harsh clipping on clouds, snow, and lava surfaces.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTonemap curve shoulder modifier.

        option.AUTO_EXPOSURE = Auto Exposure
        option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment = Dynamically adapts camera brightness as you move between dark caves and bright daylight.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSimulates eye adaptation when entering dark dungeons or emerging into the sun.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fLuminance buffer downsampling.\n§b[Tip] §7Cannot be used with OptiFine custom screenshot multipliers.

        option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_SPEED = Adaptation Speed
        option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_SPEED.comment = Controls how quickly exposure adjusts to changes in scene lighting.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values cause faster eye adaptation; lower values adapt gradually.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTemporal smoothing coefficient.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 1.00 mimics natural human eye adaptation timing.

        option.EXPOSURE = Base Exposure
        option.EXPOSURE.comment = Overall master brightness multiplier for the final image.\n\n§e[Visual] §fIncreases or decreases general scene illumination.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLinear color multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §7Adjust if your monitor is naturally dark or overly bright.

        option.MINIMUM_EXPOSURE = Minimum Exposure Floor
        option.MINIMUM_EXPOSURE.comment = Sets the darkest exposure level allowed when Auto Exposure is active.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values prevent pitch-black darkness in deep unlit caverns.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAuto exposure lower clamp.\n§b[Tip] §7Raise to 0.30+ if you find deep caves too dark to explore.

        option.TINT_R = Red Color Tint
        option.TINT_R.comment = Red color balance channel multiplier.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShift toward warm sunset, autumn, or desert tones.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

        option.TINT_G = Green Color Tint
        option.TINT_G.comment = Green color balance channel multiplier.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShift toward lush forest, jungle, or toxic atmosphere tones.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

        option.TINT_B = Blue Color Tint
        option.TINT_B.comment = Blue color balance channel multiplier.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShift toward cool alpine, winter, or ocean atmosphere tones.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

## Lighting Screen
screen.LIGHTING = Lighting & Shadows
screen.LIGHTING.comment = Sunlight and moonlight shadows, ambient occlusion, caustics, and raytracing.\n\n§e[Visual] §fConfigure real-time shadows, contact ambient shading, and global illumination.\n§c[Performance: Moderate to Heavy] §fShadow mapping is the primary GPU workload.
    option.SHADOW_MAPPING = Dynamic Shadows
    option.SHADOW_MAPPING.comment = Renders real-time dynamic shadows cast by terrain, structures, and entities from celestial light.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCasts moving sunlight and moonlight shadows that sweep across the landscape.\n§c[Performance: Heavy Impact] §fRenders an extra shadow depth pass from the sun/moon angle.\n§b[Tip] §7Disable on integrated GPUs or budget laptops for an enormous FPS boost!

    option.SHADOW_FILTER = Soft Shadow Filter
    option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment = Softens harsh, pixelated shadow edges using jittered Poisson-disk noise filtering.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates natural, smooth shadow penumbras instead of stair-stepped block edges.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fFast shadowmap multi-tap filter.\n§b[Tip] §7Highly recommended whenever Dynamic Shadows are enabled.

    option.SHADOW_COLOR = Colored Stained Glass Shadows
    option.SHADOW_COLOR.comment = Allows sunlight and moonlight to transmit colored shadows through stained glass and water.\n\n§e[Visual] §fStained glass cathedrals and tinted windows cast breathtaking colored light on floors!\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fTranslucent color shadow pass sampling.\n§b[Tip] §7Essential for beautiful cathedral builds and underwater caustics.

    option.shadowMapResolution = Shadow Resolution
    option.shadowMapResolution.comment = The texture buffer resolution used to calculate dynamic shadows (512p to 4096p).\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce razor-sharp shadow edges without pixelation.\n§c[Performance: Moderate to Heavy] §f1024p is balanced; 2048p is sharp; 4096p requires a high-end GPU.\n§b[Tip] §71024p provides excellent quality with very smooth framerates on modern cards.

    option.shadowDistance = Shadow Render Distance
    option.shadowDistance.comment = The maximum distance in blocks from the player where dynamic shadows are cast.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values render shadows on distant hills and faraway trees.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fExpands the celestial frustum volume.\n§b[Tip] §7120 to 160 blocks looks great while maintaining high performance.

    option.sunPathRotation = Sun Path Angle
    option.sunPathRotation.comment = Tilts the orbital trajectory angle of the sun and moon across the sky dome.\n\n§e[Visual] §fChanges the angle of shadows and sunlight shafts across terrain and builds.\n§a[Performance: None] §fCelestial rotation matrix calculation.\n§b[Tip] §730.0 gives iconic, dramatic diagonal lighting across the Minecraft world.

    option.ENTITY_SHADOWS = Entity Shadows
    option.ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment = Renders real-time dynamic shadows for animals, monsters, players, and boats.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCharacters and mobs cast realistic shadows on the ground below them.\n§a[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fPasses entity geometry through shadow framebuffer.\n§b[Tip] §7Turn off in crowded mob farms if you experience CPU/GPU bottlenecks.

    option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS = Block Entity Shadows
    option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment = Renders dynamic shadows for chests, bells, banners, signs, and decorative block entities.\n\n§e[Visual] §fChests and decorative blocks cast accurate shadows on floors and walls.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fPasses block entities to the shadow buffer.\n§b[Tip] §7Disable if your base contains hundreds of storage chests.

    option.SSAO = Screen Space Ambient Occlusion
    option.SSAO.comment = Calculates soft contact shadows in corners, crevices, and where blocks meet the ground.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAdds grounded depth and realistic shading to corners and foliage that lightmaps miss.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fScreen-space depth sampling with fast bilateral blur.\n§b[Tip] §7Highly recommended for grounded, natural-looking block shading.

    option.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS = Underwater Caustics
    option.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS.comment = Simulates animated light refraction webs shimmering across underwater surfaces.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDynamic sunlight webs dance on ocean floors, lake beds, and river banks.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fFast procedural noise wave refraction.\n§b[Tip] §7Requires Colored Shadows enabled for full spectrum caustics!
        value.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS.0 = OFF
        value.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS.1 = Underwater Only
        value.UNDERWATER_CAUSTICS.2 = Full (Shallow & Shore)

    option.AMBIENT_LIGHTING = Minimum Ambient Light
    option.AMBIENT_LIGHTING.comment = Sets the minimum ambient illumination level in completely unlit areas.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values brighten pitch-black caves and nighttime shadows for visibility.\n§a[Performance: None] §fConstant ambient floor scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Set to 0.05 for realistic dark caves, or 0.25+ for friendly casual visibility.

    option.WEATHER_DIRECT_LIGHT = Storm Direct Lighting
    option.WEATHER_DIRECT_LIGHT.comment = Controls sunlight and moonlight shadow intensity during rain and thunder storms.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSet to 0.00 to eliminate harsh sharp shadows during heavy downpours for realism.\n§a[Performance: None] §fWeather light scalar.\n§b[Tip] §70.00 produces an authentic, moody overcast atmosphere during rainfall.

    ## Ray Tracing Screen
    screen.RAY_TRACING = Ray Tracing & Reflections
    screen.RAY_TRACING.comment = Screen-space reflections (SSR) and screen-space global illumination (SSGI).\n\n§e[Visual] §fBrings water, metals, and smooth materials to life with mirror reflections.\n§e[Performance: Moderate to Heavy] §fRaymarching screen-space depth buffers.
        option.SSR = Screen Space Reflections (SSR)
        option.SSR.comment = Calculates real-time raymarched reflections on smooth surfaces, water, and wet blocks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fReflects surrounding terrain, builds, and skies realistically onto glossy surfaces.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fRaymarches screen depth buffer for intersection.\n§b[Tip] §7Essential for stunning water visuals and polished metallic blocks!

        option.SSGI = Global Illumination (SSGI)
        option.SSGI.comment = Experimental screen-space indirect light bouncing from bright surfaces onto dark surroundings.\n\n§e[Visual] §fColored light bounces off illuminated blocks into shadows (e.g. green grass bounce).\n§c[Performance: Heavy Impact] §fMulti-directional diffuse raymarching.\n§b[Tip] §7Experimental feature. Enable TAA for effective noise smoothing.

        option.RAYTRACER_STEPS = Raytracer Step Count
        option.RAYTRACER_STEPS.comment = Number of primary raymarching search steps across the screen buffer.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values eliminate reflection gaps and improve reflection range.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fLinear step iteration count.\n§b[Tip] §716 steps is fast and clean; 24 steps is ideal for high-end GPUs.

        option.RAYTRACER_BISTEPS = Refinement Binary Steps
        option.RAYTRACER_BISTEPS.comment = Number of binary search refinement steps executed upon ray hit confirmation.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPinpoints exact surface contact boundaries, eliminating reflection edge jitter.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fBinary search refinement.\n§b[Tip] §72 refinement steps provides razor-sharp reflection contacts at very low cost.

        option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS = Rough Surface Reflections
        option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS.comment = Simulates micro-surface roughness, diffusing and blurring reflections on non-mirror blocks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fBrushed metals, smooth stones, and damp ground show realistic blurry gloss.\n§a[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fJittered reflection ray dispersion.\n§b[Tip] §7Pairs with TAA to produce silky-smooth frosted reflections.

        option.PREVIOUS_FRAME = Previous Frame Denoising
        option.PREVIOUS_FRAME.comment = Reuses previous frame buffer color data for temporal accumulation and infinite light bounces.\n\n§e[Visual] §fStabilizes reflections and global illumination, removing temporal grain.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fTemporal history buffer lookup.\n§b[Tip] §7Keep ON for cleaner, noise-free reflections.

## Atmospherics Screen
screen.ATMOSPHERICS = Atmospherics & Sky
screen.ATMOSPHERICS.comment = Clouds, godrays, skybox, stars, Milky Way, auroras, rainbows, and meteors.\n\n§e[Visual] §fControls the heavens, celestial bodies, and dynamic atmospheric phenomena.\n§e[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fVaries with volumetric cloud and godray settings.
    option.SUN_MOON_ROUNDNESS = Sun & Moon Roundness
    option.SUN_MOON_ROUNDNESS.comment = Blends celestial bodies, stars, flares, and rainbows between square and spherical geometry.\n\n§e[Visual] §f0.00 preserves classic Minecraft squares; 0.50 gives rounded corners; 1.00 gives full circles.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAnalytical shape function.\n§b[Tip] §7Choose your aesthetic preference! 0.00 maintains pure vanilla charm.
        value.SUN_MOON_ROUNDNESS.0.00 = Square (Vanilla)
        value.SUN_MOON_ROUNDNESS.0.50 = Rounded
        value.SUN_MOON_ROUNDNESS.1.00 = Circle

    option.SUN_MOON_SIZE = Celestial Body Size
    option.SUN_MOON_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the apparent scale of the sun, moon, and End black hole in the sky.\n\n§e[Visual] §fLarger values make celestial bodies more prominent and dramatic on the horizon.\n§a[Performance: None] §fCelestial angular projection scalar.\n§b[Tip] §70.10 is perfectly proportioned with vanilla horizons.

    option.SUN_MOON_INTENSITY = Celestial Brightness
    option.SUN_MOON_INTENSITY.comment = Controls the brightness and specular glare cast by the sun and moon.\n\n§e[Visual] §fIncreases sunlight radiance and the glint of specular highlights on water.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLuminance scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Level 4 produces crisp, natural sun reflection glints.

    option.SKYBOX_BRIGHTNESS = Skybox Brightness
    option.SKYBOX_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Master brightness multiplier for the overarching sky dome gradient.\n\n§e[Visual] §fLightens or deepens daytime azure skies and nighttime cosmic backdrops.\n§a[Performance: None] §fSky color multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §71.00 matches natural vanilla sky balance.

    option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHTING = Volumetric Haze
    option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHTING.comment = Simulates physical light scattering through air moisture and atmospheric particles.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates soft atmospheric depth where distant mountains and valleys catch light.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fRaymarched atmospheric fog volume.\n§b[Tip] §7Greatly enhances landscape depth and horizon scale.

    option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHTING_STRENGTH = Volumetric Haze Density
    option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHTING_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the thickness and density of atmospheric light scattering.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create a more misty, humid, or ethereal atmosphere.\n§a[Performance: None] §fHaze density multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §70.50 provides a clean, clear atmospheric perspective.

    option.BORDER_FOG = Horizon Border Fog
    option.BORDER_FOG.comment = Blends distant terrain into the sky at the edge of your chunk render distance.\n\n§e[Visual] §fEliminates harsh chunk cutoffs with a smooth, natural horizon fade.\n§a[Performance: None] §fDistance-based fog calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Keep ON for seamless, immersive world exploration.

    option.GROUND_FOG_STRENGTH = Lowland Mist Strength
    option.GROUND_FOG_STRENGTH.comment = Adjusts the density of low-altitude ground fog that settles in valleys and river basins.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSimulates cool morning mist and swampy valley moisture.\n§a[Performance: None] §fHeight-based fog scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Looks wonderful in swamps, rivers, and deep river gorges.

    option.MILKY_WAY = Milky Way Galaxy Band
    option.MILKY_WAY.comment = Renders a stylized, procedural Minecraft-style galaxy band across the clear night sky.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFeatures glowing nebula clouds with thousands of individual twinkling stars.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fProcedural noise and analytical star clusters.\n§b[Tip] §7Turns clear nights into an awe-inspiring stargazing experience!

    option.MILKY_WAY_BRIGHTNESS = Milky Way Brightness
    option.MILKY_WAY_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Adjusts the luminous intensity of the Milky Way galaxy band.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make the cosmic dust and stars brighter and more prominent.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLuminance scalar.\n§b[Tip] §71.00 is balanced for natural night vision.

    option.AURORA = Aurora Borealis (Northern Lights)
    option.AURORA.comment = Renders volumetric dancing northern lights curtains in cold, snowy, and icy biomes.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPixelized curtains flowing from pink tops to emerald centers and electric blue bottoms!\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fProcedural raymarching in cold biomes only.\n§b[Tip] §7Appears naturally when exploring snowy plains, taigas, and frozen oceans!

    option.AURORA_BRIGHTNESS = Aurora Brightness
    option.AURORA_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Controls the glow intensity of the aurora borealis curtains.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce brighter, more luminous dancing lights in polar skies.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLuminance scalar.

    option.RAINBOW = Double Rainbow
    option.RAINBOW.comment = Renders an analytical double rainbow (or rainsquare) during rain with partial sunlight.\n\n§e[Visual] §fVivid primary bow with a fainter secondary outer bow opposite the sun or moon.\n§a[Performance: None] §fDirect analytical optical angle calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Follows your Sun/Moon Roundness setting (circle rainbow or square rainsquare!).

    option.RAINBOW_BRIGHTNESS = Rainbow Brightness
    option.RAINBOW_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Controls the color vividness and visibility of the double rainbow.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce a more saturated, prominent rainbow in the clouds.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLuminance scalar.

    option.STAR_ROTATION = Star Rotation Style
    option.STAR_ROTATION.comment = Determines the orientation angle of individual stars in the night sky and Milky Way.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAligned keeps square stars strictly axis-aligned; Random gives organic variety.\n§a[Performance: None] §fStar vertex rotation.\n§b[Tip] §7Random produces a glittering, organic diamond-like night sky!
        value.STAR_ROTATION.0 = Aligned (Grid)
        value.STAR_ROTATION.1 = Random (Organic)

    ## Godray Screen
    screen.GODRAY_SETTINGS = Godray Settings
    screen.GODRAY_SETTINGS.comment = Crepuscular rays streaming from the sun and moon through clouds and terrain.\n\n§e[Visual] §fConfigure ray sample count, beam density, and water penetration.\n§e[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fHighly optimized with adaptive step scaling.
        option.GODRAYS = Atmospheric Godrays
        option.GODRAYS.comment = Master toggle for crepuscular light shafts streaming from the sun and moon.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCasts dramatic, cinematic shafts of light through trees, clouds, and valley gaps.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fRaymarches celestial occlusion volume.\n§b[Tip] §7One of the signature visual highlights of Super Duper Vanilla!

        option.GODRAYS_QUALITY = Godray Sample Quality
        option.GODRAYS_QUALITY.comment = Number of raymarching steps taken through the shadow volume.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFast: 6 steps (smooth FPS); Balanced: 8 steps; High: 12 steps; Ultra: 16 steps.\n§e[Performance: Fast=Low, Ultra=High] §fLinear sample step count.\n§b[Tip] §7Balanced is recommended for crisp beams with silky-smooth performance.
            value.GODRAYS_QUALITY.0 = Fast (6 Steps)
            value.GODRAYS_QUALITY.1 = Balanced (8 Steps)
            value.GODRAYS_QUALITY.2 = High (12 Steps)
            value.GODRAYS_QUALITY.3 = Ultra (16 Steps)

        option.GODRAYS_DENSITY = Godray Beam Density
        option.GODRAYS_DENSITY.comment = Adjusts the brightness and visibility of the atmospheric light rays.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make light beams thicker, brighter, and more distinct.\n§a[Performance: None] §fBeam accumulation scalar.\n§b[Tip] §70.50 gives natural atmospheric subtlety; 1.00+ creates dramatic fantasy beams.

        option.GODRAYS_WATER_TRANSMISSION = Water Transmission
        option.GODRAYS_WATER_TRANSMISSION.comment = Allows godrays to penetrate and stream through translucent water and stained glass.\n\n§e[Visual] §fBeams illuminate ocean depths and cast colored shafts through cathedral glass.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fSamples secondary translucent depth buffer.\n§b[Tip] §7Disable for maximum FPS if you spend a lot of time near oceans.

        option.GODRAYS_ADAPTIVE_STEPS = Adaptive Step Optimization
        option.GODRAYS_ADAPTIVE_STEPS.comment = Dynamically concentrates ray steps where light gradient is highest near the sun.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDoubles performance when facing the sun with zero perceptible visual difference!\n§a[Performance: FPS Boost] §fIntelligently skips redundant ray steps.\n§b[Tip] §7Highly recommended to keep ON at all times!

    ## Meteor Screen
    screen.METEOR_SETTINGS = Meteor Shower Settings
    screen.METEOR_SETTINGS.comment = Dynamic procedural shooting star showers streaking across the night sky.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCustomize shower occurrence rates, speed, tail lengths, and color palettes.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fAnalytical procedural streaks calculated in the sky pass.
        option.METEORS = Meteor Showers
        option.METEORS.comment = Master toggle for procedural meteor showers in the night sky.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShooting stars ignite and streak across the stars with glowing heads and fading tails.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fLightweight analytical procedural calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Turns nighttime into an exciting celestial event!

        option.METEOR_RARITY = Shower Occurrence Rarity
        option.METEOR_RARITY.comment = Determines how frequently meteor showers occur throughout Minecraft nights.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFrom constant nightly activity to rare periodic astronomical events.\n§a[Performance: None] §fCycle threshold comparison.\n§b[Tip] §7"Regular (4-5 Nights)" makes showers feel like special, rewarding spectacles.
            value.METEOR_RARITY.0 = Every Night
            value.METEOR_RARITY.1 = Frequent (2-3 Nights)
            value.METEOR_RARITY.2 = Regular (4-5 Nights)
            value.METEOR_RARITY.3 = Rare (7-8 Nights)
            value.METEOR_RARITY.4 = Very Rare (12-15 Nights)
            value.METEOR_RARITY.5 = Lunar Cycle (New Moon)

        option.METEOR_SHOWER_STRENGTH = Meteor Frequency Rate
        option.METEOR_SHOWER_STRENGTH.comment = Controls how many meteors ignite per minute during an active shower wave.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher settings produce busy skies with multiple shooting stars at once.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTime-slice density multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §71.00 produces an authentic, natural meteor shower rate.

        option.METEOR_BRIGHTNESS = Meteor Luminous Brightness
        option.METEOR_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Controls the brightness of shooting star heads and glowing tail streaks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make streaks intensely luminous and reflective in water.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLuminance scalar.

        option.METEOR_SPEED = Meteor Flight Speed
        option.METEOR_SPEED.comment = Adjusts how rapidly meteors streak across the celestial sphere.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce lightning-fast streaks; lower values produce graceful glides.\n§a[Performance: None] §fStreak velocity scalar.

        option.METEOR_TAIL_LENGTH = Luminous Tail Length
        option.METEOR_TAIL_LENGTH.comment = Controls the physical length of the glowing ionized trail trailing behind each meteor.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create long, sweeping shooting star arcs across the sky.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTrail length scalar.

        option.METEOR_SIZE = Meteor Trail Thickness
        option.METEOR_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the thickness and pixel width of shooting star streaks.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make streaks wider and easier to spot from afar.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAngular radius scalar.

        option.METEOR_HEAD_SIZE = Leading Head Prominence
        option.METEOR_HEAD_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the size of the bright leading pixel head relative to its tail.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates an intense glowing fireball leading the ionization trail.\n§a[Performance: None] §fHead radius multiplier.

        option.METEOR_TRAIL_FADE = Trail Fade Sharpness
        option.METEOR_TRAIL_FADE.comment = Controls how crisply the meteor tail dissolves into the dark background.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values yield concentrated, sharp trails; lower values produce soft gas fades.\n§a[Performance: None] §fExponential falloff exponent.

        option.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE = Meteor Color Palette
        option.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.comment = Selects the elemental color scheme of falling shooting stars.\n\n§e[Visual] §fElectric Blue, Cosmic Violet, Emerald Green, Amber Gold, Diamond White, or Prismatic.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor palette lookup.\n§b[Tip] §7"Prismatic" gives each falling meteor a unique random gemstone color!
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.0 = Electric Blue
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.1 = Cosmic Violet
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.2 = Emerald Green
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.3 = Amber Gold
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.4 = Diamond White
            value.METEOR_COLOR_PROFILE.5 = Prismatic (Multicolor)

        option.METEOR_WAVE_VARIATION = Shower Activity Rhythm
        option.METEOR_WAVE_VARIATION.comment = Dictates how shower activity waxes and wanes over the course of the night.\n\n§e[Visual] §fConstant maintains a steady stream; Dynamic produces calm lulls followed by peak bursts!\n§a[Performance: None] §fModulation waveform.\n§b[Tip] §7"Dynamic Waves" mimics real astronomical Perseid/Leonid meteor peaks.
            value.METEOR_WAVE_VARIATION.0 = Constant
            value.METEOR_WAVE_VARIATION.1 = Dynamic Waves

        option.METEOR_SKY_COVERAGE = Sky Distribution Area
        option.METEOR_SKY_COVERAGE.comment = Dictates where in the sky dome meteors are allowed to ignite and streak.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFull Sky covers all horizons; Stream focuses south; Radiant clusters near origin.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAngular masking filter.\n§b[Tip] §7"Full Sky" gives the most immersive panoramic experience.
            value.METEOR_SKY_COVERAGE.0 = Full Sky (Panoramic)
            value.METEOR_SKY_COVERAGE.1 = Directional Stream
            value.METEOR_SKY_COVERAGE.2 = Radiant Focused

        option.METEOR_RADIANT_SPREAD = Radiant Origin Size
        option.METEOR_RADIANT_SPREAD.comment = Adjusts the angular diameter of the radiant area from which meteors stream outward.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSmaller values make meteors radiate from a tighter point in space.\n§a[Performance: None] §fRadiant dispersion angle.

        option.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION = Radiant Origin Quadrant
        option.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.comment = Selects the compass quadrant in the sky from which meteors appear to originate.\n\n§e[Visual] §fLike snow rushing past a windshield, streaks radiate outward from this direction.\n§a[Performance: None] §fCelestial vector anchor.
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.0 = North-East
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.1 = North-West
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.2 = South-East
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.3 = South-West
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.4 = Zenith (Overhead)
            value.METEOR_RADIANT_DIRECTION.5 = Celestial (Following Moon)

    ## Lightning Screen
    screen.LIGHTNING_SETTINGS = Lightning & Flashes
    screen.LIGHTNING_SETTINGS.comment = Configure lightning flash dynamics, cloud-to-cloud discharges, internal cloud illumination, and photosensitivity safety.\n\n§e[Visual] §fRealistic short flashes, subtle multi-stroke strobe effects, intra-cloud crawler bolts, and glowing cloud scattering.\n§c[Health Warning] §fIncludes photosensitivity / epilepsy safety protection to completely disable all flashing lights.

        option.EPILEPSY_SAFETY = Photosensitivity Safety
        option.EPILEPSY_SAFETY.comment = §c[!] EPILEPSY & PHOTOSENSITIVITY WARNING§r\n§fThis shader features dynamic lightning flashes, cloud-to-cloud discharges, and strobing effects that may trigger seizures for individuals with photosensitive epilepsy.\n\n§a[ON] §fCompletely disables ALL flashing lights, lightning sky flashes, cloud-to-cloud flashes, internal cloud glows, and End dimension flashes across the entire shader pack.\n§c[OFF] §fDynamic lightning flashes and strobe effects are active.\n\n§eRecommended for anyone sensitive to sudden bright flashes.
            value.EPILEPSY_SAFETY.true = §aSafe (No Flashing Lights)
            value.EPILEPSY_SAFETY.false = §cStandard (Flashes Active)

        option.LIGHTNING_FLASH = Lightning Flash Mode
        option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment = §c[Warning: Flashing Lights] §fControls the duration and dynamics of lightning sky flashes.\n\n§eOff: §fDisables screen flashes while keeping bolts visible.\n§eRealistic Short: §fFast, punchy, realistic flashes that reach peak brightness instantly and decay rapidly in milliseconds (~150ms).\n§eSmooth Fade: §fSofter, more gradual illumination falloff.
            value.LIGHTNING_FLASH.0 = Off
            value.LIGHTNING_FLASH.1 = Realistic Short
            value.LIGHTNING_FLASH.2 = Smooth Fade

        option.LIGHTNING_STROBE = Lightning Strobe Effect
        option.LIGHTNING_STROBE.comment = §c[Warning: Flashing Lights] §fEnables a slight, natural multi-stroke strobe effect that occurs on some lightning strikes (~38% of discharges).\n\n§e[Visual] §fSimulates rapid atmospheric re-strikes (dart leaders) with 1 to 2 subtle, fast restrikes (spaced ~65ms apart) for authentic lightning flutter.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAnalytical temporal waveform.\n§b[Tip] §7Happens occasionally, just like real thunderstorms!

        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING = Cloud-to-Cloud Lightning
        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING.comment = Enables horizontal and diagonal cloud-to-cloud crawler lightning discharges traversing the cloud deck during storms.\n\n§e[Style] §f100% faithful to vanilla Minecraft's iconic geometric segmented line aesthetic with sharp polygonal kinks, enriched with detailed branching.\n§b[Silent] §fPurely visual in the shader with zero audio noise/sound.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fAnalytical segmented ray test with fast bounding cull.

        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_BRANCHES = Lightning Branching Details
        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_BRANCHES.comment = Configures the geometric branch hierarchy and detail density for cloud-to-cloud lightning.\n\n§eClassic: §fMain trunk with primary fork branches.\n§eDetailed: §fTrunk with primary forks and secondary tendril branches.\n§eIntricate: §fExtensive spider-branching crawler lightning spreading across the cloud deck.
            value.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_BRANCHES.1 = Classic
            value.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_BRANCHES.2 = Detailed
            value.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_BRANCHES.3 = Intricate Spider

        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_GLOW = Cloud Internal Glow
        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_GLOW.comment = Illuminates the clouds from within with dynamic volumetric scattering whenever lightning discharges occur.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDense cloud billows trap and scatter the electric light, lighting up the cloud mass from the inside out.\n§a[Performance: None] §fInternal cloud scattering modulation.

        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_FREQUENCY = Lightning Frequency
        option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING_FREQUENCY.comment = Multiplier for how often cloud-to-cloud lightning discharges occur during thunderstorms.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce more frequent crawler bolts and glowing intra-cloud flashes.

        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_R = Lightning Red
        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_R.comment = Red color component for all lightning bolts, cloud-to-cloud flashes, internal cloud glows, celestial illumination, flares, and godrays.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDefault 240 provides a dazzling purple-ish white balance when combined with blue.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_G = Lightning Green
        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_G.comment = Green color component for all lightning bolts, cloud-to-cloud flashes, internal cloud glows, celestial illumination, flares, and godrays.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDefault 225 provides brilliant clarity, luminescence, and natural atmospheric radiance.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_B = Lightning Blue
        option.LIGHTNING_COLOR_B.comment = Blue color component for all lightning bolts, cloud-to-cloud flashes, internal cloud glows, celestial illumination, flares, and godrays.\n\n§e[Visual] §fDefault 255 provides rich electric violet and purple-ish white radiance.\n§a[Performance: None] §fColor channel scalar.

    ## Cloud Screen
    screen.CLOUD_SETTINGS = Cloud Settings
    screen.CLOUD_SETTINGS.comment = Volumetric 3D, skybox, and vanilla clouds with procedural weather dynamics.\n\n§e[Visual] §fConfigure cloud layers, altitude, thickness, softness, and weather responsiveness.\n§e[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fVolumetric mode requires raymarching steps.
        option.CLOUD_TYPE = Cloud Rendering Mode
        option.CLOUD_TYPE.comment = Selects the cloud rendering architecture.\n\n§e[Visual] §fVanilla: classic blocky clouds; Skybox: fast 2D plane; Volumetric: realistic 3D volume.\n§e[Performance: Vanilla=None, Volumetric=Moderate] §fRaymarched depth density.\n§b[Tip] §7Volumetric clouds look incredible and are highly optimized!
            value.CLOUD_TYPE.0 = Vanilla
            value.CLOUD_TYPE.1 = Skybox
            value.CLOUD_TYPE.2 = Volumetric 3D

        option.DYNAMIC_WEATHER = Procedural Dynamic Weather
        option.DYNAMIC_WEATHER.comment = Simulates an organic, procedural multi-day weather and cloud coverage cycle.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSky coverage ranges from totally clear blue skies to overcast and moody storm fronts.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fProcedural noise weather clock.\n§b[Tip] §7Allows rain to happen during overcast skies instead of vanilla instant transitions.

        option.STATIC_OVERCAST = Static Overcast Level
        option.STATIC_OVERCAST.comment = Sets the permanent overcast parameter when Procedural Dynamic Weather is disabled.\n\n§e[Visual] §fLocks cloud cover and overcast atmosphere to a permanent level.\n§a[Performance: None] §fFixed overcast scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Setting to 0.40–0.60 allows beautiful sunlit rain and procedural rainbows during vanilla rainfall!
            value.STATIC_OVERCAST.-1.00 = Dynamic (Vanilla)
            value.STATIC_OVERCAST.0.00 = 0% (Clear Sky)
            value.STATIC_OVERCAST.0.50 = 50%
            value.STATIC_OVERCAST.1.00 = 100% (Overcast)

        option.DYNAMIC_CLOUDS = Dynamic Cloud Motion
        option.DYNAMIC_CLOUDS.comment = Allows clouds to evolve, shift shape, and respond dynamically to wind speed.\n\n§e[Visual] §fClouds gently morph and drift naturally across the sky.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fNoise coordinate translation.\n§b[Tip] §7Works beautifully on both vanilla and volumetric cloud types.

        option.DOUBLE_LAYERED_CLOUDS = High-Altitude Cirrus Clouds
        option.DOUBLE_LAYERED_CLOUDS.comment = Renders a secondary, wispy cloud deck high in the stratosphere above normal clouds.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAdds great atmospheric depth with high-altitude cirrus clouds drifting overhead.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fEvaluates secondary cloud layer.\n§b[Tip] §7Brings immense vertical scale and realism to the sky.

        option.STORY_MODE_CLOUDS = Story Mode Cloud Styling
        option.STORY_MODE_CLOUDS.comment = Softens clouds with a gentle vertical fade inspired by Minecraft: Story Mode.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFades smoothly from an opaque base to a translucent, airy top with extra thickness.\n§a[Performance: None] §fVertical gradient density filter.\n§b[Tip] §7Gives clouds a delightful, stylized storybook aesthetic!

        option.SOFT_CLOUD_EDGE = Rounded Cloud Edges
        option.SOFT_CLOUD_EDGE.comment = Smooths and rounds the outer block boundaries of clouds.\n\n§e[Visual] §fReplaces hard, sharp blocky cloud borders with soft, pillowy curves.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fDistance field smoothing.\n§b[Tip] §7Great if you want a softer, less rigid look while keeping voxel charm.

        option.FADE_SPEED = Cloud Morphing Speed
        option.FADE_SPEED.comment = Adjusts how rapidly clouds shift shape and morph as they drift.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce faster evolving cloud formations.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTime scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 0.20 provides calm, relaxing cloud movement.

        option.SECOND_CLOUD_HEIGHT = Cirrus Layer Altitude
        option.SECOND_CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment = Sets the height offset for the secondary high-altitude cirrus cloud deck.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPositions the upper cloud layer higher or lower in the sky.\n§a[Performance: None] §fHeight coordinate offset.

        option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUD_STEPS = Volumetric Cloud Steps
        option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUD_STEPS.comment = Number of raymarching sample steps for 3D volumetric clouds.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values improve cloud density precision and eliminate step banding.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fSample step count.\n§b[Tip] §716 steps is fast and clean; 32 steps is ultra smooth.

        option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUD_DEPTH = Volumetric Cloud Thickness
        option.VOLUMETRIC_CLOUD_DEPTH.comment = Determines the physical vertical thickness of volumetric clouds.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values make clouds thicker, heavier, and more voluminous.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLayer height bounds.

        option.SKYBOX_CLOUD_STEPS = Skybox Cloud Steps
        option.SKYBOX_CLOUD_STEPS.comment = Raymarching sample count for the Skybox cloud mode.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values improve cloud definition when using the Skybox cloud type.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fSample step count.

        option.SKYBOX_CLOUD_DEPTH = Skybox Cloud Thickness
        option.SKYBOX_CLOUD_DEPTH.comment = Vertical thickness bounds for the Skybox cloud mode.\n\n§e[Visual] §fAdjusts cloud layer vertical presence.\n§a[Performance: None] §fLayer bounds scalar.

## World Screen
screen.WORLD = World & Waving
screen.WORLD.comment = Waving foliage, plant animations, flowing water, wind speed, and world curvature.\n\n§e[Visual] §fMakes the world feel alive with gentle breezes and animated vegetation.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fVertex shader animations with negligible overhead.
    option.TERRAIN_ANIMATION = Waving Foliage & Plants
    option.TERRAIN_ANIMATION.comment = Simulates wind gently blowing through grass, leaves, flowers, crops, and vines.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPlants, leaves, and hanging lanterns sway naturally in the breeze.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fFast vertex displacement shader.\n§b[Tip] §7Instantly brings life and organic movement to landscapes!

    option.WATER_ANIMATION = Waving Water Surface
    option.WATER_ANIMATION.comment = Animates undulating surface waves and ripples across oceans, lakes, and rivers.\n\n§e[Visual] §fWater surfaces rise and fall with realistic fluid waves.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fVertex wave height displacement.\n§b[Tip] §7Looks spectacular when catching sun and moon reflections.

    option.WEATHER_ANIMATION = Waving Weather Particles
    option.WEATHER_ANIMATION.comment = Applies wind physics and diagonal gusts to falling rain and snow particles.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPrecipitation slants and drifts dynamically with the prevailing wind.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fPrecipitation particle displacement.

    option.TIMELAPSE_MODE = Timelapse Smooth Animation
    option.TIMELAPSE_MODE.comment = Synchronizes animation speeds to in-game world time rather than real frame time.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFoliage and water speeds accelerate naturally during time-lapses or time commands!\n§a[Performance: None] §fUniform time source substitution.\n§b[Tip] §7Perfect for recording stunning day/night cycle time-lapses!
        value.TIMELAPSE_MODE.0 = OFF
        value.TIMELAPSE_MODE.1 = Fragment Only (Water & Sky)
        value.TIMELAPSE_MODE.2 = Full (Water, Sky & Foliage)

    option.WIND_SPEED = Wind Velocity
    option.WIND_SPEED.comment = Controls how fast plants, leaves, lanterns, and weather sway in the breeze.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce faster, stormier foliage movement.\n§a[Performance: None] §fAnimation phase multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §71.00 gives a relaxing, gentle natural breeze.

    option.CURRENT_SPEED = Liquid Flow Speed
    option.CURRENT_SPEED.comment = Adjusts the animation and flow speed of water and underwater sea grass.\n\n§e[Visual] §fControls how swiftly ocean currents and rivers appear to move.\n§a[Performance: None] §fFluid phase multiplier.

    option.WIND_FREQUENCY = Wind Gust Frequency
    option.WIND_FREQUENCY.comment = Controls the frequency of wind gusts and wave direction changes.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values cause quicker, more frequent fluttering of leaves.\n§a[Performance: None] §fSpatial noise frequency.

    option.CURRENT_FREQUENCY = Liquid Wave Frequency
    option.CURRENT_FREQUENCY.comment = Controls the spatial wave frequency of water ripples and currents.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create tighter, choppier surface ripples.\n§a[Performance: None] §fWave frequency scalar.

    option.WORLD_CURVATURE = Planet World Curvature
    option.WORLD_CURVATURE.comment = Curving vertex shader that renders the Minecraft world as a small planet or sphere!\n\n§e[Visual] §fDistant terrain curves away beneath the horizon like Animal Crossing or Mario Galaxy.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fVertex quadratic displacement.\n§b[Tip] §7Fun, quirky, and creates uniquely whimsical landscape perspectives!

    option.WORLD_CURVATURE_SIZE = Curvature Radius
    option.WORLD_CURVATURE_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the radius of the curved planet world.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSmaller values curve more tightly; negative values invert into a bowl shape!\n§a[Performance: None] §fCurvature radius scalar.

## PBR & Materials Screen
screen.PBR = Materials & PBR
screen.PBR.comment = Physically Based Rendering, specular highlights, water, lava, sculk, and POM.\n\n§e[Visual] §fConfigure material reflections, surface relief, and custom fluid shaders.\n§a[Performance: Low to Moderate] §fPOM (Parallax) is the main performance factor.
    option.PBR_MODE = PBR Material Mode
    option.PBR_MODE.comment = Enables Physically Based Rendering, granting blocks realistic roughness and reflectivity.\n\n§e[Visual] §fIntegrated PBR generates materials from vanilla textures; LabPBR uses installed PBR resource packs.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fEvaluates material properties during deferred shading.\n§b[Tip] §7Integrated PBR looks fantastic on pure vanilla textures with zero extra setup!
        value.PBR_MODE.0 = OFF
        value.PBR_MODE.1 = Integrated PBR (Auto Vanilla)
        value.PBR_MODE.2 = LabPBR 1.3 (Resource Pack)

    option.SPECULAR_HIGHLIGHTS = Specular Sun Glint
    option.SPECULAR_HIGHLIGHTS.comment = Renders sun and moon specular reflection glints on smooth and metallic surfaces.\n\n§e[Visual] §fPolished blocks, metals, and wet ground catch bright glints from the sun and moon.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fCook-Torrance or Blinn-Phong specular calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Essential for bringing metallic and polished stone textures to life.

    option.ENVIRONMENT_PBR = Environmental Wetness & Rain
    option.ENVIRONMENT_PBR.comment = Simulates dynamic moisture, rain puddles, and dampness on exposed blocks during rain.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSurfaces glisten and show dampness when rained upon, drying up when clear.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fRain wetness material factor.\n§b[Tip] §7Adds incredible atmosphere when weather fronts roll through!

    option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING = Subsurface Scattering (SSS)
    option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING.comment = Simulates sunlight penetrating and softly illuminating the backsides of translucent leaves.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFoliage and leaves glow vibrantly when backlit by morning and evening sunbeams.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fTranslucency backlighting calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Makes tree canopies and forests feel remarkably lush and radiant!

    option.EMISSIVE_INTENSITY = Emissive Block Brightness
    option.EMISSIVE_INTENSITY.comment = Multiplier for glowing blocks like redstone, glowstone, magma, and glowing ores.\n\n§e[Visual] §fControls how brightly glowing block textures appear in the dark.\n§a[Performance: None] §fEmissive color scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Level 8 gives rich, luminous ore and crystal accents.

    option.NORMAL_STRENGTH = Normal Map Depth Strength
    option.NORMAL_STRENGTH.comment = Controls the strength of 3D surface bumps and crevices from normal maps.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values create more pronounced depth on stone, bricks, and bark.\n§a[Performance: None] §fNormal vector tangent perturbation scalar.

    option.NORMAL_GENERATION = Auto-Generated Normal Maps
    option.NORMAL_GENERATION.comment = Automatically generates 3D normal depth maps for standard vanilla textures.\n\n§e[Visual] §fGives vanilla cobblestone, wood planks, and brick surfaces 3D tactile relief!\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fReal-time Sobel gradient filter across albedo textures.\n§b[Tip] §7Enjoy realistic 3D block relief without installing heavy resource packs!

    option.NORMAL_GENERATION_RESOLUTION = Auto-Normal Resolution
    option.NORMAL_GENERATION_RESOLUTION.comment = Internal texture sampling resolution for auto-generated normal maps.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce finer, crisper micro-relief details.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fTexture coordinate sampling scale.\n§b[Tip] §7128 is crisp and perfectly balanced for vanilla textures.

    option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS = Directional Torchlight Relief
    option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS.comment = Casts directional relief shadows from handheld and placed torches across normal maps.\n\n§e[Visual] §fTorchlight creates realistic cast shadows across brick mortar and rough stone!\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fLightmap gradient normal dot product.\n§b[Tip] §7Looks stunning when exploring caves with a handheld torch.

    option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAP_STRENGTH = Directional Light Strength
    option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAP_STRENGTH.comment = Intensity of the directional relief shading cast by torchlight.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce deeper, more dramatic surface shadows from torches.\n§a[Performance: None] §fIntensity scalar.

    option.SLOPE_NORMALS = Sloped Edge Normals
    option.SLOPE_NORMALS.comment = Generates smooth beveled normal lighting across block edges and stairs.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSoftens harsh cube corners with subtle beveled edge reflections.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fGeometric normal calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Disable if using a high-resolution 3D resource pack.

    ## POM Screen
    screen.POM_SETTINGS = Parallax Occlusion (POM)
    screen.POM_SETTINGS.comment = True 3D depth and self-shadowing simulated on flat block textures.\n\n§e[Visual] §fTurns flat texture bricks, cobblestone, and tiles into true recessed 3D geometry!\n§c[Performance: Moderate to Heavy] §fRequires step raymarching through heightmaps.
        option.PARALLAX_OCCLUSION = Parallax Occlusion Mapping
        option.PARALLAX_OCCLUSION.comment = Raymarches into surface heightmaps to simulate real 3D geometry depth.\n\n§e[Visual] §fMortar sinks into bricks, gravel stones pop out, and wood planks have true grooves.\n§c[Performance: Heavy Impact] §fRaymarching per-pixel heightmaps.\n§b[Tip] §7Requires a LabPBR resource pack with heightmaps enabled.

        option.PARALLAX_DEPTH = Parallax Depth Scale
        option.PARALLAX_DEPTH.comment = Maximum simulated depth distance into the block surface.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce deeper recesses and bolder 3D relief.\n§a[Performance: None] §fHeightmap depth scalar.

        option.PARALLAX_STEPS = Parallax Sample Steps
        option.PARALLAX_STEPS.comment = Number of raymarching steps taken to find the surface depth intersection.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values eliminate stair-step layer artifacts on steep angles.\n§c[Performance: Heavy Impact] §fLoop iteration count.\n§b[Tip] §7128 steps is the sweet spot for crisp 3D relief without FPS drop.

        option.PARALLAX_SHADOW = Parallax Self-Shadowing
        option.PARALLAX_SHADOW.comment = Allows raised 3D features to cast tiny realistic shadows onto recessed areas.\n\n§e[Visual] §fBricks cast self-shadows into the mortar grooves as the sun moves!\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fSecondary raymarch toward celestial light.\n§b[Tip] §7Adds incredible micro-detail realism to textured surfaces.

        option.PARALLAX_SHADOW_STEPS = Parallax Shadow Steps
        option.PARALLAX_SHADOW_STEPS.comment = Number of shadow ray steps taken toward the light source.\n\n§e[Visual] §fHigher values produce cleaner, more accurate micro self-shadows.\n§e[Performance: Moderate Impact] §fSecondary loop step count.

    ## Water Screen
    screen.WATER_SETTINGS = Water Material Settings
    screen.WATER_SETTINGS.comment = Water clarity, noise distortion, wave normals, absorption, foam, and colors.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCustomize how oceans, lakes, and rivers look and flow.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fOptimized procedural water shader.
        option.WATER_STYLE = Water Aesthetic Style
        option.WATER_STYLE.comment = Selects the water visual presentation style.\n\n§e[Vanilla] §fRich, saturated water color with gentle reflections and higher opacity. Gives water real substance and lets modded effects like boat wakes, splash decals, and foam pop cleanly.\n§e[Realistic] §fCrystal-clear tropical water with mirror-like glassy reflections and high transparency.\n§a[Performance: None] §fVisual material style.\n§b[Tip] §7Vanilla is the new default designed for maximum mod compatibility (Wakes, Effective, etc.)!
        value.WATER_STYLE.0 = Realistic
        value.WATER_STYLE.1 = Vanilla

        option.WATER_NOISE = Water Surface Noise
        option.WATER_NOISE.comment = Adds procedural animated noise variation to water transparency and brightness.\n\n§e[Visual] §fBreaks up repetitive water textures with natural organic patches.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fProcedural noise calculation.\n§b[Tip] §7Inspired by the beloved Super Duper Graphics Pack water style!

        option.WATER_BRIGHTNESS = Water Clarity Brightness
        option.WATER_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Controls overall water brightness and transparency luminance.\n\n§e[Visual] §fLower values create deep, rich sapphire oceans; higher values create crystal clear springs.\n§a[Performance: None] §fBrightness scalar.\n§b[Tip] §71.00 provides crystal-clear tropical visibility.

        option.WATER_NORMAL = Water Wave Normals
        option.WATER_NORMAL.comment = Enables 3D animated normal map wave crests across liquid surfaces.\n\n§e[Visual] §fProduces realistic surface ripples that glint in the sun and moon.\n§a[Performance: Low Impact] §fEvaluates normal map derivative.\n§b[Tip] §7Essential for realistic, shimmering lake and ocean surfaces.

        option.WATER_BLUR_SIZE = Wave Smoothness Blur
        option.WATER_BLUR_SIZE.comment = Adjusts the smoothness and blur radius of water surface waves.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSmaller values create sharp, crisp ripples; larger values create smooth ocean swells.\n§a[Performance: None] §fNormal map filtering kernel size.

        option.WATER_DEPTH_SIZE = Wave Depth Relief
        option.WATER_DEPTH_SIZE.comment = Controls the perceived 3D height and depth of water ripples.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSmaller values increase wave contrast and perceived height.\n§a[Performance: None] §fWave normal depth multiplier.

        option.WATER_TILE_SIZE = Water Texture Scale
        option.WATER_TILE_SIZE.comment = Controls the repeating grid scale of the water wave pattern.\n\n§e[Visual] §fSmaller values make waves finer; larger values make broad ocean swells.\n§a[Performance: None] §fUV coordinate multiplier.\n§b[Tip] §7Default 16 matches standard Minecraft block proportions.

        option.WATER_STYLIZE_ABSORPTION = Depth Color Absorption
        option.WATER_STYLIZE_ABSORPTION.comment = Simulates physical light absorption through water depth.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShallow water remains crystal clear while deep ocean trenches turn deep sapphire navy.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fExponential depth absorption math.\n§b[Tip] §7Creates breathtaking natural transitions from sandy shores to deep seas!

        option.WATER_FOAM = Shore & Entity Foam
        option.WATER_FOAM.comment = Renders animated sea foam where water laps against beaches, rocks, and swimming mobs.\n\n§e[Visual] §fFrothy white foam lines form along shores, boats, and submerged structures.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fDepth edge proximity intersection.\n§b[Tip] §7Adds vibrant coastal life to oceans and beaches!

        option.WATER_FLAT = Flat Water Albedo
        option.WATER_FLAT.comment = Replaces textured water color with a clean, flat stylized albedo tone.\n\n§e[Visual] §fCreates an ultra-clean, minimalist modern water appearance.\n§a[Performance: None] §fTexture bypass toggle.

        option.WATER_DEPTH_WAVES = Depth Waves & Puddles
        option.WATER_DEPTH_WAVES.comment = Dynamically scales wave amplitude with water depth, softening ripples in shallow ponds and completely flattening waves on solid blocks or modded puddles.\n\n§e[Visual] §fShallow ponds remain peaceful and clear, while puddles on solid ground form still, mirror-like surfaces without artificial waves or foam.\n§a[Performance: Very Low] §fDepth-buffer wave amplitude scalar.\n§b[Tip] §7Perfect compatibility for puddle mods (Puddles & Floods, etc.) and peaceful shallow water!

    ## Lava Screen
    screen.LAVA_SETTINGS = Lava Material Settings
